    <text:soft-page-break/>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="TableLine105553233396992">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table1.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:list xml:id="list74820606180877" text:continue-numbering="true" text:style-name="L1">
       <text:list-item>
        <text:p text:style-name="P19">In the dialog that appears, mark those awards for which you wish to solicit votes. <text:s/>For each such award, decide how many votes each person may cast for that award. <text:s/>(Bear in mind that young racers are likely to be tempted to vote for themselves. <text:s/>One strategy for dealing with that is to allow them to vote for multiple distinct candidates: they might waste one vote on their own car, but their remaining votes would identify truly deserving recipients.)</text:p>
       </text:list-item>
      </text:list>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table1.B2" office:value-type="string">
